    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §88, Nav L",
    "lawSection": "Navigation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8270\n\nSPONSOR: SAVINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the navigation law, in relation to the base pilotage\ntariffs at Sandy Hook, Sands Point and Execution Rocks\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nIncreases the base pilotage tariffs at Sandy Hook, Sands Point and\nExecution Rocks.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends Section 88 of the Navigation Law to adjust the\npilotage tariff table over a five-year period commencing January 1,\n2023. The rates increase by the following percentage each year: 3%, 3%,\n3%, 3% and 3% plus a 1.5% surcharge on vessels above 1650 pilotage\nunits.\n\nSection 1 amends item (A) of subclause 1 of clause (ii) of subparagraph\n1 of paragraph (h) of subdivision 4 of section 88 of the navigation law,\nto establish five new tariff tables, the first is effective January 1,\n2023. Each subsequent table replaces its predecessor effective a year\nthereafter.\n\nSection 2 provides that the bill takes effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAdjusting the tariff schedule recognizes the change in the nature of\nvessels utilizing the Port. When the schedule was established 34 years\nago, vessel size was well within the established limits.  However,\nduring that time, vessels have doubled in size and can accommodate much\nmore cargo. Therefore, the total number of ships has decreased while\ntotal tonnage and value of cargo has increased.\n\nSchedule adjustments are necessary to compensate for the resulting\ndecreased. revenue stream thereby enabling the pilots to maintain their\nhistorically exemplary level of service.\n\nThe increase is necessary to allow the Sandy Hook pilots to expand\neducational programs for pilots, fund the cost of newly added employees\nand increased operational expenses such as insurance and fuel, and to\nmaintain the integrity of the pilot base which was completely rebuilt\nfollowing Superstorm Sandy.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill  \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
